{"title":"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each principal of Lincoln High School serves exactly one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-year term. What is the maximum number of principals this school could have during an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-year period?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fb35752e07ec6682630baf1d22cae4bb87545ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the current principal's term will end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> year.  Of the next <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> years, the current principal will serve the first year; the next principal will serve the second, third, and fourth years; a third principal will serve the fifth, sixth, and seventh years; and a fourth principal will serve the eighth year.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different principals will serve in the next <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> years.\n</p><p>Consider a period that includes at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different principals.  During this period, all principals except the first and last must serve complete terms. So at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> principals serve complete terms, and thus this period is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> years long.  Therefore, an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-year period may not have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or more different principals.\n</p><p>Thus there can be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723b429af793af50b01f31ed8467bba78553c55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> principals in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-year period.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-year period, at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cda15777410a4bf4b5eb332cce67302e5f8e486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor{\\frac{8}{3}}\\right\\rfloor = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"45\" /> principals could serve complete terms.  Furthermore, at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> principals could serve incomplete terms during this period: those who are in office at the start and end of this period.  Therefore, at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/935b1992f07f8955c663ab2264d31ed3341eb4c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"121\" height=\"30\" /> principals could be active during this period (which would happen if the acting principal at the start of the period has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> year left of their term).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 8\">2000 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2000 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span cl